\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Awake, our souls! Away, our fears!
\par Let every trembling thought be gone!
\par Awake, and run the heavenly race,
\par And put a cheerful courage on.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. True, 'tis a strait and thorny road,
\par And mortal spirits tire and faint;
\par But they forget the mighty God
\par That feeds the strength of every saint.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O mighty God, Thy matchless power,
\par Is ever new and ever young,
\par And firm endures, while endless years
\par Their everlasting circles run.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. From Thee, the ever flowing spring,
\par Our souls shall drink a fresh supply;
\par While such as trust their native strength
\par Shall melt away, and droop, and die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Swift as the eagle cuts the air,
\par We'll mount aloft to Thine abode;
\par On wings of love our souls shall fly,
\par Nor tire along the heavenly road.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

